  "question": {
    "text": "If $x=\\int_0^y \\frac{d t}{\\sqrt{1+t^2}}$, then $\\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}$ is equal to :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "bOPlF",
      "text": "\n$y$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "wTBKM",
      "text": "\n$\\sqrt{1+y^2}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "oh9nC",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{1+y^2}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "31EUV",
      "text": "\n$y^2$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$x=\\int_0^y \\frac{d t}{\\sqrt{1+t^2}}$\n$\\Rightarrow 1=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1+y^2}} \\cdot \\frac{d y}{d x}$\n$\\left[\\because\\right.$ If $\\mathrm{I}(x)=\\int_{\\phi(x)}^{\\psi(x)} f(t) d t$, then $\\frac{d \\mathrm{I}(x)}{d x}=f\\{\\psi(x)\\}$\n$\\frac{\\mathrm{dy}}{\\mathrm{dx}}=\\sqrt{1-\\mathrm{y}^2}$\n$\\frac{d^2 y}{d x^2}=\\frac{1}{2 \\sqrt{1+y^2}} \\cdot 2 y \\cdot \\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{y}{\\sqrt{1+y^2}} \\cdot \\sqrt{1+y^2}=y$",
    "image": null
  },
